NETWORK USE
-----------

Section 13 of the AGPL applies to this project because it is normally operated
as a network service. If you run a modified version of ConfPilot and let other
people use it over a network, you must offer those users the Corresponding
Source of your modified version.

Running an unmodified copy creates no additional obligation beyond keeping the
license and copyright notices intact. Operators of modified instances should
publish their source and link to it from the running application. See
docs/licensing.md for what this means in practice.


THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------

ConfPilot depends on third-party packages distributed under their own licenses.
Those licenses continue to govern those components; this project's license
applies to ConfPilot's own source.

The exact production dependency graph resolved from pnpm-lock.yaml and the full
license text shipped by each production package are checked into
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. The current production graph is MIT-licensed. Installed
development dependencies are also audited against the lockfile and the
reviewed-compatible license list.

Reproduce this list with:

    pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
    node scripts/audit-licenses.mjs

After an intentional lockfile update, regenerate and review the checked-in
notice with `node scripts/audit-licenses.mjs --write-notice`.
